course: dictionary
lesson: 2551
title: Degrade: when things get worse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «About a third of the world's soils are degraded by erosion, salt, pollution or overuse.» Degraded here means damaged and made worse, so the soil is no longer as healthy as it should be. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Damaged fits, so degrade means to make something worse.
explain: Degrade can also mean to break down slowly into smaller, simpler parts. Science lessons use it this way: plastic takes hundreds of years to degrade. The clue is the time. Something that takes hundreds of years is changing very slowly.
explain: Degrade can also mean treating someone without respect, so that they feel worthless. Here the clue is in the feeling: «it degrades people to be shouted at» tells you that being shouted at makes people feel small and worthless.
explain: The words around degrade tell you which meaning to choose. Soil, pollution and land point to damage. Plastic and bacteria point to breaking down. People and feelings point to respect. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Degrade is a verb: degrade, degrades, degraded, degrading.
fact: «Degrade» can mean to make something worse in quality or condition.
fact: In science, «degrade» means to break down slowly into smaller, simpler parts.
fact: «Degrading» treatment means treating someone without respect, so they feel worthless.
fact: Biodegradable materials can be broken down by living things, such as bacteria.
exercise: «About a third of the world's soils are degraded by erosion, salt, pollution or overuse.» What does degraded mean here? | *Made worse or damaged | Made very wet and cold | Made into a park | Made into a bed
exercise: «Plastic takes hundreds of years to degrade.» What does degrade mean in this sentence? | *Break down slowly into smaller parts | Grow very fast | Shine brightly | Melt into a hot liquid at once
exercise: Which word means that living things like bacteria can break it down? | Shiny | Unbreakable | *Biodegradable | Waterproof
test: «It degrades people to be shouted at.» What does degrades mean here? | Makes them sound like a bell | Makes them glow in the dark | *Treats them without respect, so they feel worthless | Makes them taller
test: «Pollution degrades the land and the rivers.» Which word could replace degrades? | Cleans | Paints | Measures | *Damages and makes worse
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The forest was degraded by years of fires»? | Made into a bridge | Made quieter | Made taller | *Made worse or damaged
